  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "note": "EF Core as opaque persistence: handing an entity to a DbContext or DbSet reads it deep and writes its own fields, since tracking may set keys and navigations. Saving, querying and transactions touch nothing; context state is no resource until phase 5e. Model configuration, migrations, registration, ExecuteAsync with its delegate and loaders writing unnamed navigations are not known. An entity or collection handed over gets a deep read and a write of the argument.",
